            {
                "box": {
                    "code": "\r\n// Puckette's vcf~ from Pd by pete for evieve\r\n\r\ncosQ73(x) {\n\tc1 =  0.999999953464;\n\tc2 = -0.499999053455;\n\tc3 =  0.0416635846769;\n\tc4 = -0.0013853704264;\n\tc5 =  0.00002315393167;  \t\n\n\tx2 = x * x;\n\treturn (c1 + x2 * (c2 + x2 * (c3 + x2 * (c4 + c5 * x2))));\n}\n\r\n// optimised version: x is already clamped to 0.. and at audio rate\r\n// 6 muls at any one time, plus the branching\r\ncos73nc(x) {\n\t// get quadrant # (0 to 2) we're in\r\n\tquad = int(x * 0.63661977236758);// 2 / pi\n\tcosreturn = 0;\n\tif \t\t\t\t(quad == 0) {\n\t\tcosreturn =  cosQ73(x);\n\t} else if \t\t(quad == 1) {\n\t\tcosreturn = -cosQ73(pi - x);\n\t} else if \t\t(quad == 2) {\t// we only might reach the 3rd quadrant\n\t\tcosreturn = -cosQ73(x - pi);\n\t} else {\t//\t(quad == 3)\t\t// we never reach the 4th quadrant here\n\t\tcosreturn =  cosQ73(twopi - x);\n\t}\n\treturn cosreturn;\n}\n\r\nsin73nc(x) {\n\treturn cos73nc(halfpi - x);\n}\r\n\r\n// [vcf~] from Pd is just a direct form 2 solved for sin()\r\n// (this is basically just [bp~] but a bit better)\r\npd_vcf(x0, hz)\r\n{\r\n\tHistory\tb1(0), b2(0);\r\n\tParam\tq(sqrt2, min=0.1);\r\n\r\n\todq\t= 1 / q;\r\n\tcf\t= hz * twopi / samplerate;\r\n\tr\t= maximum((1 - cf * odq), 0);\r\n\r\n\ta1\t= cos73nc(cf) * r;\t// cf needs up to pi rather than just halfpi\r\n\ta2\t= sin73nc(cf) * r;\r\n\r\n\tbp\t= ((x0 * (1 - r) * (2 - 2 / (q + 2))) + (b1 * a1)) - (b2 * a2);\r\n\tlp\t=  (b1 * a2) + (a1 * b2);\r\n\thp\t=  (x0 - (q * bp) - lp) * odq;\r\n\r\n\tb1\t= bp;\r\n\tb2\t= lp;\r\n\r\n\treturn bp, lp, hp;\t\t// real, imaginary, pete\r\n}\r\n\r\nParam\tq(sqrt2, min=0.1, max=10000);\t// max ?\r\n\r\n// in terms of Hz (\"in 2\"), anything above (samplerate/twopi)\r\n// can be a bit funky if q is low, depending on filter type\r\n// but still much larger and more stable range than [bp~]\r\nhz\t\t= clamp(in2, 0.01, 18000);\r\n\r\nout1, out2, out3\t= pd_vcf(in1, hz, q=q);\r\n// others: peak = (hp - lp), broken notch = (hp + lp)\r\n\r\n",
                    "fontface": 0,
                    "fontname": "<Monospaced>",
                    "fontsize": 12.0,
